P4 (typography) is in place and ticked in `tasks.md`. Typecheck and lint are clean, and `pnpm test` passes 248/248. The e2e specs I ran pass 22/22 after a fresh build. They were the new `typography-p4` spec (10 tests) plus `landing-r4`, `theme-tokens-p2`, `scaffold`, `vertical-slice`, `wafer-stage-r6`, `bin-pareto-task10` and `yield-summary-task11`.

**What changed**
- **Type tokens (`src/app/globals.css`):** every §4.2 style now has its size, line-height and letter-spacing as CSS variables, plus a `.type-*` class. New classes are `title-1`, `stat-s`, `row-title` and `subhead`.
- **Breakpoints:** the verdict headline steps from 48 to 44 px below 1440 and to 36 px below 1280. Stats drop to 32 px below 1280. The mobile sizes now start below 640 px instead of 768.
- **Global font settings:** `html` sets `"cv11", "ss03"`, optical sizing, font smoothing and `optimizeLegibility`. The `opsz` 32 setting is on display and stat roles. Numbers are tabular everywhere except the two display sizes.
- **CJK (§4.3):** letter-spacing is 0 on every token, with the §4.3 line-heights and display sizes. A leftover `-0.02em` rule on stats in CJK is gone. `li` elements now get the same text-wrap rules as `p`.
- **Class renames and changes:** `type-footnote` is now `type-subhead` in every component. `title-3` is now weight 400 and `title-2` is 24 px, which changes the landing page, so both landing screenshots were re-captured.
- **Findings:** the finding headline and possible-cause title use `row-title`, and the finding sub-line uses `subhead`.
- **TypeScript tokens:** `TYPOGRAPHY_TOKENS` in `src/ui/tokens/tokens.ts` now mirrors §4.2, and the CJK values are updated.

**Tests**
- `src/ui/tokens/typography-tokens.test.ts` checks the token table and the CSS against §4.2 and §4.3.
- `e2e/typography-p4.spec.ts` checks the computed styles of the verdict headline, stat value, finding headline and finding sub-line at 1440 and 390. It also runs the A40 check: letter-spacing is 0 and the line-break rules apply in `ja`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW` and `ko` at both widths.

**Choices I made where premium.md is silent (also in `logs/progress.md`)**
- **640–1023 px:** the 1024 sizes (headline 36, stat 32) apply all the way down to 640.
- **Verdict step-down:** I kept the current behaviour: it still triggers at 2 lines and steps down once. The §4.3 three-line rule belongs to P17. The stepped-down size is now `min(40px, display-l)`, so at 1024 it can't grow from 36 to 40.
- **Magnifier:** one 11 px glyph is left for P23.

Evidence is recorded in `logs/premium-acceptance.md`.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=201

